{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526612-what-clans-did-you-hate-at-first-but-warmed-up-later","id":1526612,"title":"What clans did you hate at first but warmed up later?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-12-10T10:54:54-08:00","id":1526612,"title":"What clans did you hate at first but warmed up later?","content":"A fun question I wanted to ask.<br /> <br /> For me it was the Ventrue as I read what they were like in the Dark Ages and started to get a better respect for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T12:17:22-08:00","id":1526621,"title":"","content":"Ventrue as well! Though I still prefer Ventrue <i>antitribu</i> to the diet clan. the knightly role just works so well for them - reminds me of how fluff for 1st edition stated Ventrue often avoided the position of Prince, preferring to serve as advisors or viziers.<br /> <br /> I've also grown somewhat fond of Malkavians, though my vision of the clan is perhaps closer to the depiction of the Ravnos. Trickster archetypes and illusion magic are always fun, once you get past the Fishmalk stereotype.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28177-gamiem","name":"gamiem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T13:57:54-08:00","id":1526626,"title":"","content":"Toreador, Ventrue, and Tremere all came across to high school me as essentially the popular kids I disliked. As I got older and the clans were expanded on in the Dark Ages and Revised material, I came to enjoy them quite a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T14:41:22-08:00","id":1526629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gamiem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526612-what-clans-did-you-hate-at-first-but-warmed-up-later?p=1526621#post1526621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ventrue as well! Though I still prefer Ventrue <i>antitribu</i> to the diet clan. the knightly role just works so well for them - reminds me of how fluff for 1st edition stated Ventrue often avoided the position of Prince, preferring to serve as advisors or viziers.<br /> <br /> I've also grown somewhat fond of Malkavians, though my vision of the clan is perhaps closer to the depiction of the Ravnos. Trickster archetypes and illusion magic are always fun, once you get past the Fishmalk stereotype.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also strongly prefer the knightly Ventrue. I have a Ventrue elder who is in the Camarilla who is a diablerist hunter/knight-errant in the modern day and it's very fun to roleplay that character. He's beside himself with disgust to see what his clan has become while at the same time feeling like a relic of the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2204-toreador","name":"Toreador","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2204_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-11T03:30:32-08:00","id":1526669,"title":"","content":"Tzimisce. First I saw them as a brutal clan dedicated to create Frankensteins. Later, more material was made and the noblesse oblige of the clan is fascinating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-11T04:31:45-08:00","id":1526672,"title":"","content":"With me it was the Gangrel and the Nosferatu at first glance they were one thing and then you see that there is much more to them and their way of being than their condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-12T11:48:16-08:00","id":1526709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gamiem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526612-what-clans-did-you-hate-at-first-but-warmed-up-later?p=1526621#post1526621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ventrue as well! Though I still prefer Ventrue <i>antitribu</i> to the diet clan. the knightly role just works so well for them - reminds me of how fluff for 1st edition stated Ventrue often avoided the position of Prince, preferring to serve as advisors or viziers.<br /> <br /> I've also grown somewhat fond of Malkavians, though my vision of the clan is perhaps closer to the depiction of the Ravnos. Trickster archetypes and illusion magic are always fun, once you get past the Fishmalk stereotype.</div> </div> </div> </div>To expand on the latter, I like the idea of 'fae vampires' on an aesthetic level; as I only ever use the original seven clans in my chronicles and write-ups, Malkavians got their fair share of Ravnos and Kiasyd in my deconstruction of the supplementary clans into the original seven. I've toyed with the idea of <i>making</i> Malkavians the Changelings of the setting - compare the insinuations in the early editions that Sabbat Gangrel were responsible for myths of werewolves. A simple approach would be making Camarilla Malkavians an equivalent of the Seelie Court and the Malkavian <i>antitribu</i> an equivalent of the Unseelie Court; though, what implications would this have for cross-Sect interactions between Malkavians? Choices, choices...<br /> <br /> Though their association with mental illness would not be removed <i>per se </i>(not that it needs to be, anyway), it would give the clan a strong identity that complements and <i>surpasses</i> their current box of 'mentally ill vampires'; what myth or trope are the Malkavians supposed to be referencing, anyway? Is there such a thing as a Dracula or Lestat for Malkavians?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28177-gamiem","name":"gamiem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-12T19:32:44-08:00","id":1526728,"title":"","content":"I had the opposite issue.<br /> <br /> I loved the Tremere when I first started playing the game, but then as the writers kept using them as the plot point for everything and loading more and more mechanics bloat for Thaumaturgy, I became quite disillusioned with them.<br /> <br /> The Tremere turned themselves into vampires and in just a few centuries drove one major clan to extinction, subjugated a clan of vampire assassins, created a new bloodline of vampires, survived vampire wars with three large clans, helped form the Camarilla, and despite everything they have done they are too useful to kill.<br /> <br /> The Toreador clan on the other hand has spent the last 7,000 years role playing &quot;The Devil Wears Prada&quot;, the Gangrel have spent the last 7,000 years in emo yiffing piles, the Ventrue ran Rome and the Brujah ran Carthage.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-14T15:46:07-08:00","id":1526819,"title":"","content":"I came around to Malkavians.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-14T17:49:35-08:00","id":1526823,"title":"","content":"I've always been more of a lover than a hater so I can't claim to have ever hated or disliked one Clan or another. Some held more interest for me than others at start but right now I'm pretty much good with all of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T09:35:29-08:00","id":1526854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526612-what-clans-did-you-hate-at-first-but-warmed-up-later?p=1526819#post1526819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I came around to Malkavians.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always liked this clan and tried to view them as tricksters &amp; at times cruel jesters that would speak uncomfortable truth to the leading kindred of any given region and tried not to depict them as a clan of the Jokers of DC Comics even though the Joker is my favorite DC baddie and I admit it took me time to get the depiction right and not be a case of bad comedy that Galavtron would say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T09:50:27-08:00","id":1526860,"title":"","content":"I'm kind of with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"970\" data-vbnamecard=\"970\">Gurkhal</a> in that I can't really say that I ever <i>hated</i> any of the Clans. But the Tzimisce are probably one of my favourite Clans now, and that definitely wasn't the case to begin with.<br /> <br /> I've also really warmed up to Malkavians a lot: I think it's partially starting with the very extreme example from Bloodlines as a baseline. But it also probably involved a bit of &quot;I see myself in this picture and I don't like it&quot; as well, where I had to get a bit more comfortable with my own weird brain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T23:36:43-08:00","id":1526901,"title":"","content":"Interestingly, how certain clans are PLAYED isn't necessarily what the TEXT says about them.<br /> <br /> * Brujah are played as the dumb muscle of the Camarilla despite the fact they go out of their way to embrace smart people and leaders.<br /> <br /> * Gangrel tend to be portrayed as Berserkers, Druids, or Rangers versus genuine hardened survivors at all costs.<br /> <br /> * Malkavians are played as Batman villains, tricksters, and illusionists despite the fact this is the Ravnos thing.<br /> <br /> * Nosferatu are generally treated as exaggerated carnival folk and personalities versus secretive and mysterious.<br /> <br /> * The Tremere are often power hungry schemers despite the books emphasizing they eschew temporal power for magical.<br /> <br /> * Toreador...okay, Toreador are portrayed pretty much as written but most STs let them actually make art.<br /> <br /> * Ventrue are always played as complete tools despite the fact they are supposed to be so charismatic they have two social disciplines.<br /> <br /> * Ravnos are basically played as either Gambit or Exotic Dancer GirlTM.<br /> <br /> * The Giovanni were never able to shed the mafia image despite only one family being that way.<br /> <br /> * The Setites really go all in on the whole Egyptian Thulsa Doom thing even when it was shown otherwise.<br /> <br /> * The Banu Haqim is admittedly something that has zig zagged from its original cult origins so I'm not sure what IS the way they're written these days.<br /> <br /> * The Lasombra are always played as essentially sexy European aristocrats versus Social Darwinist psychopaths.<br /> <br /> * The Tzimisce are either played as Dracula or Rob Zombie villains.<br /> <br /> * The Salubri are always played as antitribu because everyone hates the canon Goodie-Goodies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T23:37:55-08:00","id":1526902,"title":"","content":"Double post","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 12-16-2023, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-16T11:55:13-08:00","id":1526932,"title":"","content":"Strange how that goes CTPhipps. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-16T11:57:37-08:00","id":1526933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526612-what-clans-did-you-hate-at-first-but-warmed-up-later?p=1526823#post1526823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always been more of a lover than a hater so I can't claim to have ever hated or disliked one Clan or another. Some held more interest for me than others at start but right now I'm pretty much good with all of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could never really get into the Ravnos clan myself and thought the Malkavians were a better suited to the role tricksters and illusionists and upsetting the balance of power in any fiefdom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-16T11:58:57-08:00","id":1526934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526612-what-clans-did-you-hate-at-first-but-warmed-up-later?p=1526860#post1526860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm kind of with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"970\" data-vbnamecard=\"970\">Gurkhal</a> in that I can't really say that I ever <i>hated</i> any of the Clans. But the Tzimisce are probably one of my favourite Clans now, and that definitely wasn't the case to begin with.<br /> <br /> I've also really warmed up to Malkavians a lot: I think it's partially starting with the very extreme example from Bloodlines as a baseline. But it also probably involved a bit of &quot;I see myself in this picture and I don't like it&quot; as well, where I had to get a bit more comfortable with my own weird brain.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't go far wrong liking the Malkavians and the Tzimisce lines, but I preferred the Old Clan faction over the mainstream clan myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-16T15:31:44-08:00","id":1526947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526612-what-clans-did-you-hate-at-first-but-warmed-up-later?p=1526901#post1526901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Ventrue are always played as complete tools despite the fact they are supposed to be so charismatic they have two social disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this has less to do with the way they are written vs played, than it has to do with the fact that some types of characters can't be faked regardless of system. You need a baseline to really play them well.<br /> <br /> I have seen this many times where someone really wants to play a character which specializes in something they themselves can't really pull off. The socially inept person who wants to be the socialite, the meek player who wants to try playing the bully, the small picture person who wants to play the 4D chess big picture power player, etc. I know it sounds harsh, but lets be honest here, if you have never cooked or watched someone cook, chances are you will try to grab a hot pan without an oven mitt.<br /> <br /> With Ventrue, you are supposed to read the room, and be empathetic enough to be who ever you need to be to get the other person to follow your lead. But a lot of people just look at Dominate and note the those with high Dominate scores often have low empathy, and just lean into that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-16T15:38:32-08:00","id":1526948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526612-what-clans-did-you-hate-at-first-but-warmed-up-later?p=1526934#post1526934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can't go far wrong liking the Malkavians and the Tzimisce lines, but I preferred the Old Clan faction over the mainstream clan myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's actually a minor scandal apparently how the Tzimisce fandom is sharply divided on those lines.<br /> <br /> Some people believe Vicissitude is everything.<br /> <br /> Others believe Vicissitude is the least interesting part of the Clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-16T16:59:52-08:00","id":1526951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526612-what-clans-did-you-hate-at-first-but-warmed-up-later?p=1526948#post1526948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's actually a minor scandal apparently how the Tzimisce fandom is sharply divided on those lines.<br /> <br /> Some people believe Vicissitude is everything.<br /> <br /> Others believe Vicissitude is the least interesting part of the Clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'm the one that loves all the li'l monsters equally <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-17T15:22:15-08:00","id":1527004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526612-what-clans-did-you-hate-at-first-but-warmed-up-later?p=1526901#post1526901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Malkavians are played as Batman villains, tricksters, and illusionists despite the fact this is the Ravnos thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always point prospective Malk players to the Greek mythology about Cassandra. Usually the first, easiest way to get them understanding the assignment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * Toreador...okay, Toreador are portrayed pretty much as written but most STs let them actually make art. </div> </div> </div>This is one clan where players highly benefit from seeing them played, or playing them, off-type. I admit this is one clan I personally hated until I played one, went out of my way to throw every Toreador stereotype on its nose, and ended up with this character who was a complete sleazeball cat burglar/art thief.<br /> <br /> <i>Now</i> I realize they're actually a fun clan (to play off-type) with one of the most ridiculously overpowered discipline sets in the game. Sure, they don't hold a candle to either Telyav or Szantovich in that regard, but for a full clan opposed to obscure bloodline...not bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * Ventrue are always played as complete tools despite the fact they are supposed to be so charismatic they have two social disciplines. </div> </div> </div>I feel like a lot of that springs from game mechanics. The fluff is full of badass frontline leaders who lead by example and are capable of shrugging off wounds that would kill lesser vampires, but in actual play Ventrue tend to crumple like wet paper bags against so much as a stiff breeze. It strikes me that provokes players to run them as douche-y cowards, opposed to leaders who put their money where their mouths are.<br /> <br /> I've mentioned my house rules elsewhere on the forums (and this isn't the place to go into them), but even a little bit of minor combat balance tweaking makes Ventrue absolutely <i>horrifying</i> to face, and completely true to what fluff makes them out to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * Ravnos are basically played as either Gambit or Exotic Dancer GirlTM.<br /> <br /> * The Giovanni were never able to shed the mafia image despite only one family being that way.<br /> <br /> * The Setites really go all in on the whole Egyptian Thulsa Doom thing even when it was shown otherwise.<br /> <br /> * The Banu Haqim is admittedly something that has zig zagged from its original cult origins so I'm not sure what IS the way they're written these days. </div> </div> </div>I love the smell of uncomfortable cultural baggage in the morning. It smells like...a flame war.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * The Lasombra are always played as essentially sexy European aristocrats versus Social Darwinist psychopaths. </div> </div> </div>Look at who the major Lasombra metaplot characters are. That ain't exactly players' faults.<br /> <br /> For my part, I just tell players they're Sith lords. Right down to the whole &quot;strike me down with all of your hatred&quot; ethos. That's it, there's really not a whole lot else to explain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * The Tzimisce are either played as Dracula or Rob Zombie villains. </div> </div> </div>To be fair, that's how they were set up in older editions before <i>good</i> lore about the old clan got published.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 12-17-2023, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-17T21:07:59-08:00","id":1527032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526612-what-clans-did-you-hate-at-first-but-warmed-up-later?p=1526933#post1526933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could never really get into the Ravnos clan myself and thought the Malkavians were a better suited to the role tricksters and illusionists and upsetting the balance of power in any fiefdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is of course true to a degree although to be honest I haven't a very firm opinion on the Ravnos. I see Ravnos more as agents of chaos rather than tricksters or such, as tricksters gives a way to pleasent vibe for a Clan of Cainites. But like I said I have no firm opinion about the Ravnos so this view will likely change or evolve in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-17T21:37:27-08:00","id":1527033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526612-what-clans-did-you-hate-at-first-but-warmed-up-later?p=1527032#post1527032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is of course true to a degree although to be honest I haven't a very firm opinion on the Ravnos. I see Ravnos more as agents of chaos rather than tricksters or such, as tricksters gives a way to pleasent vibe for a Clan of Cainites. But like I said I have no firm opinion about the Ravnos so this view will likely change or evolve in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cultural baggage aside, they seem to have settled onto Ravnos as the Clan of Thieves (which doesn't really shed the Gambit image) rather than &quot;Indian subcontinent Clan&quot; or &quot;Romani Stereotype Clan.&quot;<br /> <br /> We'll see if it sticks to the landing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-19T04:17:36-08:00","id":1527081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526612-what-clans-did-you-hate-at-first-but-warmed-up-later?p=1527033#post1527033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cultural baggage aside, they seem to have settled onto Ravnos as the Clan of Thieves (which doesn't really shed the Gambit image) rather than &quot;Indian subcontinent Clan&quot; or &quot;Romani Stereotype Clan.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit, I much prefer their secondary, mercenary, niche: couriers, messengers, scouts, spies, cross-domain information brokers, and roaming fixers/problem solvers. With most clans and bloodlines known for mercenary behavior being fully aligned to sects, integrated into clans, or written out of v5, it gives the Ravnos a distinct niche and potential role within a chronicle -- especially with the new anti-technology doctrine espoused by the Camarilla, a minority of Anarchs, and some Independents.<br /> <br /> And by coincidence, it fleshes out the Gangrel/Ravnos beef beyond Uncomfortable Cultural Baggage: they're competing for the same &quot;ecological&quot; niche.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-19T05:42:34-08:00","id":1527082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526612-what-clans-did-you-hate-at-first-but-warmed-up-later?p=1526728#post1526728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had the opposite issue.<br /> <br /> I loved the Tremere when I first started playing the game, but then as the writers kept using them as the plot point for everything and loading more and more mechanics bloat for Thaumaturgy, I became quite disillusioned with them..</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always thought the Tremere to so <i>obviously</i> be a better analogue for the Dracula kind of vampire than either the Ventrue or the Tzimisce. A clan of elitist warrior-scholars who turned themselves into vampires through black magic and keep their progeny in a state of permanent bondage is quite literally the character of Dracula expanded into a vampire ethnicity. At least the Count's status as a Tremere is clear in my homebrew setting.<br /> <br /> (I associate the Ventrue with Tony Scott's <i>The Hunger</i> - of course)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28177-gamiem","name":"gamiem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-19T17:16:27-08:00","id":1527098,"title":"","content":"Ravnos as agents of chaos I could get behind Gurkhal rather then being tricksters and thieves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T07:33:26-08:00","id":1527770,"title":"","content":"Tremere. First I thought they where a brain wishing shadow council cult but then I realized they are mostly just shut in book nerds wanting to study in peace and ensuring via the pyramid to be mostly safe of internal struggles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}